//! The node core: composes the DAG + GHOSTDAG + consensus-strict relay + mempool + miner into one
//! object with three verbs a running node needs:
//!   * [`Node::ingest_tx`]  — accept a gossiped PQ tx into the mempool.
//!   * [`Node::ingest_block`] — accept a gossiped block (consensus-validated + orphan-buffered graft).
//!   * [`Node::produce`]    — build a block template on the current tips + mempool and graft it as
//!     this node's own block, returning it for the transport to gossip. Because the template is
//!     built from tips the node already holds, ANY node can produce — no single producer.
//!
//! The libp2p_ffi onion transport (feeds ingest_* on inbound gossip, pushes produce()'s block), the
//! PoW-grind engine (fills nonce/pow_bind on the template, #73), and the ZK-proof
//! consensus verify (the usdm-decider WHIR light decider) wire onto this same object in the following bricks.

/// ⭐ KASPA'S SPENDABILITY (lane speed5, 2026-11-19): how many fold steps under the newest fold step a send's member leg anchors
/// (`Node::final_fold_step`). 2 clears the measured re-order at the newest step (A-F36) at ~7 s on the live run-2 pace.
pub(crate) const SPEND_ANCHOR_DEPTH: u64 = 2;

