#[cfg(test)]
thread_local! {
    /// THE OWN-TRANSACTION EMBARGO IN A UNIT TEST (found 2026-11-10: twelve pins red since a19f584f, 2026-11-07). A node
    /// keeps a transaction one of its own wallets built out of its own templates until the network echoes it, or for 60 to
    /// 120 s of WALL time (`Node::hold_own_tx`), so its block never names the sender's node. A two-node pin has no network
    /// to echo and cannot wait a minute, so every pin of the shape "A publishes, A produces, B grafts" produced a block
    /// that carried nothing and then read the object as never applied. Off by default on a test thread: the fixture
    /// models the echo as already heard. The embargo's own pin turns it on ([`embargo_own_txs_for_test`]) and measures
    /// the hold and the release. Production has no such switch.
    static OWN_TX_EMBARGO_FOR_TEST: std::cell::Cell<bool> = const { std::cell::Cell::new(false) };
    /// THE FINAL FOLD STEP IN A UNIT TEST (A-F25, 2026-11-11). On a real chain an object's member leg is anchored at the
    /// newest FINAL fold step (`Node::final_fold_step`: the bonded set's votes, or 64 steps of depth). An in-process
    /// fixture has no bonded set voting and folds a handful of steps, so by that rule it would never name a final step and
    /// no pin could build an object at all. Off by default on a test thread: the fixture models every folded step as
    /// final (nothing in it re-orders a step unless the pin does so itself). The final anchor's own pins turn the real
    /// rule on ([`measure_final_step_for_test`]) and measure both arms and the wait. Production has no such switch.
    static FINAL_STEP_MEASURED_FOR_TEST: std::cell::Cell<bool> = const { std::cell::Cell::new(false) };
    /// DB-310 test instrument: how many held records a span-close fold re-derived on this thread (thread-local, so
    /// parallel tests never see each other's count).
    static SPAN_CLOSE_DERIVES: std::cell::Cell<u64> = const { std::cell::Cell::new(0) };
    /// DB-440 test instrument: how many positions a span-close fold stepped on this thread (every root it folded, sealed,
    /// derived or the candidate) — the walk's whole cost, which DB-310's derive count does not see.
    static SPAN_FOLD_STEPS: std::cell::Cell<u64> = const { std::cell::Cell::new(0) };
    /// Span-seal test instrument: how many record roots a ladder span seal re-derived from held record bytes on this
    /// thread (`Node::span_seal_root`) — the term that held the runtime lock 11.5 s per 4,096-record seal.
    static SPAN_SEAL_DERIVES: std::cell::Cell<u64> = const { std::cell::Cell::new(0) };
}

